WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.136
-You know, our next guest
from "Saturday Night Live."

00:00:03.136 --> 00:00:06.840
She also produces, writes,
and stars in the show "Shrill."

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:09.242
All episodes of
the third and final season

00:00:09.242 --> 00:00:11.244
will be on Hulu this Friday.

00:00:11.244 --> 00:00:14.714
Everyone, please welcome
Aidy Bryant!

00:00:14.714 --> 00:00:16.616
-♪ It's Aidy Bryant ♪

00:00:16.616 --> 00:00:18.884
♪ And she's dressed to kill ♪

00:00:18.884 --> 00:00:20.887
♪ She's mighty, mighty ♪

00:00:20.887 --> 00:00:23.189
♪ On that show called "Shrill" ♪

00:00:23.189 --> 00:00:25.057
♪ It's Aidy Bryant ♪

00:00:25.057 --> 00:00:27.359
♪ It's her turn to drive ♪

00:00:27.359 --> 00:00:29.062
♪ Up to the eighth floor ♪

00:00:29.062 --> 00:00:31.230
♪ On "Saturday Night Live" ♪

00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:33.432
♪ Yeah ♪

00:00:33.432 --> 00:00:37.069
-That's gotta feel good, right?
-Ohh. So nice!

00:00:37.069 --> 00:00:39.305
Wow! It's really nice
to have a crowd.

00:00:39.305 --> 00:00:41.374
-It's amazing, right?
-Yeah.

00:00:41.374 --> 00:00:43.776
-As a performer,
this -- it's everything.

00:00:43.776 --> 00:00:45.244
-You need 'em.
-It's everything.

00:00:45.244 --> 00:00:47.280
-We need ya.
-Yeah, we totally do.

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:49.682
Thank you so much
for coming on the show.

00:00:49.682 --> 00:00:52.685
I know you're busy. You got
a new show this Saturday.

00:00:52.685 --> 00:00:54.687
I gotta say
you're crushing it this season.

00:00:54.687 --> 00:00:56.088
-Oh, thanks!
-And I will say

00:00:56.088 --> 00:00:58.657
that my favorite thing so far
that you're doing now --

00:00:58.657 --> 00:01:01.394
This new character you're doing.
Ted Cruz.

00:01:01.394 --> 00:01:03.663
-Yeah.
-[ Laughter ]

00:01:03.663 --> 00:01:06.366
-This is when he came back
from Cancun. [ Laughs ]

00:01:06.366 --> 00:01:09.101
-Yeah.

00:01:09.101 --> 00:01:11.704
-Did you know you had
a Ted Cruz in you?

00:01:11.704 --> 00:01:13.473
And what --

00:01:13.473 --> 00:01:15.442
-I -- I still am amazed

00:01:15.442 --> 00:01:17.476
that I'm finding him every day
in there.

00:01:17.476 --> 00:01:19.412
Um, no. I didn't know.

00:01:19.412 --> 00:01:21.381
And, also, I didn't --
You know, normally,

00:01:21.381 --> 00:01:22.815
like, sometimes during the week,

00:01:22.815 --> 00:01:25.084
you have an idea
that an impression is coming up.

00:01:25.084 --> 00:01:27.086
And him in particular,

00:01:27.086 --> 00:01:29.588
it kind of, like,
sprung up on us on Friday.

00:01:29.588 --> 00:01:31.791
And so, Saturday morning
I went in, and they were like,

00:01:31.791 --> 00:01:33.126
"You have Ted Cruz. Okay."

00:01:33.126 --> 00:01:34.427
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:01:34.427 --> 00:01:36.396
-Isn't that wild?
-I just was like, "Okay.

00:01:36.396 --> 00:01:38.198
I'll put something
together, but..."

00:01:38.198 --> 00:01:40.165
And then I felt like, okay,

00:01:40.165 --> 00:01:42.535
well, that'll be my only time
I did Ted Cruz.

00:01:42.535 --> 00:01:45.238
And then it was, like,
week after week.

00:01:45.238 --> 00:01:46.939
They were like,
"Get the beard out!"

00:01:46.939 --> 00:01:49.442
-"Get the beard back out!
People want to hear the hits!

00:01:49.442 --> 00:01:51.710
They want the Ted Cruz."
Yeah, exactly.

00:01:51.710 --> 00:01:54.046
Because you're doing that,
as well as "Shrill,"

00:01:54.046 --> 00:01:55.881
which, by the way,
congratulations.

00:01:55.881 --> 00:01:58.151
It comes out on Friday.
-Yeah.

00:01:58.151 --> 00:02:01.120
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:02.955
-All the episodes on Friday,

00:02:02.955 --> 00:02:05.057
but Friday is also
your birthday, by the way.

00:02:05.057 --> 00:02:07.560
-I know!
-Happy birthday!

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:09.128
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:09.128 --> 00:02:11.397
-Thank you. Thank you.
-Happy, happy birthday!

00:02:11.397 --> 00:02:13.565
-You know, yeah, it's a lot.

00:02:13.565 --> 00:02:17.269
It's a lot of attention
for me on one day, I think.

00:02:17.269 --> 00:02:19.372
I'm scared that I'll never
be the same afterwards.

00:02:19.372 --> 00:02:21.274
-Yeah, I mean,
you couldn't plan this

00:02:21.274 --> 00:02:23.309
if you planned it
four years in advance.

00:02:23.309 --> 00:02:25.811
-No, I -- It was not my idea.
I want people to know that.

00:02:25.811 --> 00:02:27.580
That was --
They just chose the date.

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:29.315
And I was like,
"That's my birthday."

00:02:29.315 --> 00:02:32.218
And they were like,
"Okay. We don't care." Um...

00:02:32.218 --> 00:02:34.687
-This season, I know you --
There was an episode

00:02:34.687 --> 00:02:36.923
where you had to learn
the Electric Slide.

00:02:36.923 --> 00:02:38.290
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:02:38.290 --> 00:02:39.892
-And you were talking to me
about this.

00:02:39.892 --> 00:02:42.528
Now, why did it bother you?
Or not bother you.

00:02:42.528 --> 00:02:44.230
But why is it still
in your brain that you --

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:47.966
-No, I think it was -- It became
a big moment for me in my life.

00:02:47.966 --> 00:02:49.369
-All right. Explain this.

00:02:49.369 --> 00:02:51.137
-Well, you know,

00:02:51.137 --> 00:02:53.472
you think you know
the Electric Slide, don't ya?

00:02:53.472 --> 00:02:55.207
-Of course. Yeah.
We all know it.

00:02:55.207 --> 00:02:57.610
-You've all been to a wedding
or a bat mitzvah.

00:02:57.610 --> 00:02:59.712
You know --
You know the Electric Slide.

00:02:59.712 --> 00:03:00.913
-Yes.
-Well, so, we wrote it

00:03:00.913 --> 00:03:02.615
into the show.

00:03:02.615 --> 00:03:04.316
It was like, okay,
this girls' night out.

00:03:04.316 --> 00:03:06.352
The four girls are going to do
the Electric Slide.

00:03:06.352 --> 00:03:08.254
And the director,
Carrie Brownstein, was like,

00:03:08.254 --> 00:03:09.856
"I think we should get
a choreographer

00:03:09.856 --> 00:03:11.824
just so you guys look
really tight and all together."

00:03:11.824 --> 00:03:14.427
And in my mind, I was like,
"Okay, lady.

00:03:14.427 --> 00:03:16.895
We don't need a choreographer.
We know it."

00:03:16.895 --> 00:03:18.597
-Yeah, it's the Electric Slide.

00:03:18.597 --> 00:03:20.666
-And so they got
the choreographer.

00:03:20.666 --> 00:03:22.167
And it just so happened that,

00:03:22.167 --> 00:03:23.836
like, when we were
supposed to rehearse,

00:03:23.836 --> 00:03:25.338
I had an issue with my costume,

00:03:25.338 --> 00:03:27.406
so the other girls
went and rehearsed.

00:03:27.406 --> 00:03:30.109
And then right when I could
join them, they were done.

00:03:30.109 --> 00:03:32.144
And then it was just me

00:03:32.144 --> 00:03:36.082
and a professional choreographer
in a huge room.

00:03:36.082 --> 00:03:38.918
And it was like,
"Do the Electric Slide."

00:03:38.918 --> 00:03:40.486
-That's pressure.

00:03:40.486 --> 00:03:43.622
-And it was
the most intimate, raw,

00:03:43.622 --> 00:03:47.259
nightmarish pain I've ever felt
in my entire life.

00:03:47.259 --> 00:03:48.994
And suddenly I found myself
being like,

00:03:48.994 --> 00:03:51.129
"What is the Grapevine?
What is a little shimmy?"

00:03:51.129 --> 00:03:55.167
Like, I'm -- Raw terror
looking into this man's eye.

00:03:55.167 --> 00:03:56.836
-"I've done this
a million times.

00:03:56.836 --> 00:03:58.003
Is this the Electric Slide?"

00:03:58.003 --> 00:04:00.039
-So then I think
because of that,

00:04:00.039 --> 00:04:03.442
he was like, "This woman doesn't
know the Electric Slide.

00:04:03.442 --> 00:04:05.111
She needs extra help."

00:04:05.111 --> 00:04:07.146
I would say, for 20 minutes,

00:04:07.146 --> 00:04:11.417
I quietly did the Electric Slide
for a professional choreographer

00:04:11.417 --> 00:04:13.719
probably 10 times in a row.

00:04:13.719 --> 00:04:16.755
Solo Electric Slide?

00:04:16.755 --> 00:04:18.824
It will chill you
to your damn bones.

00:04:18.824 --> 00:04:20.059
-All right. Yeah. We get that.

00:04:20.059 --> 00:04:22.061
-But I survived.
-You survived. You did it.

00:04:22.061 --> 00:04:24.597
-It looked great on camera.
Oh, wow.

00:04:24.597 --> 00:04:27.132
-You film the show
in and around Portland.

00:04:27.132 --> 00:04:29.001
-Yeah.
-Gosh. That's --

00:04:29.001 --> 00:04:30.502
-It's the best.
-That's a cool place.

00:04:30.502 --> 00:04:32.805
-And it's, like, such
a cool town to explore.

00:04:32.805 --> 00:04:35.207
And we went, like,
all these areas around it.

00:04:35.207 --> 00:04:36.408
We went to the beach.

00:04:36.408 --> 00:04:38.577
We went to this cattle ranch
we shot on.

00:04:38.577 --> 00:04:40.713
-Oh, yeah.
-And -- Yeah.

00:04:40.713 --> 00:04:42.615
There's, like, a scene
where we shot at this

00:04:42.615 --> 00:04:45.652
full-working cattle ranch,
and we thought it would be funny

00:04:45.652 --> 00:04:49.088
to write in that a child
on an ATV comes

00:04:49.088 --> 00:04:52.324
and picks me up and takes me
across the cattle ranch.

00:04:52.324 --> 00:04:54.961
But I didn't realize that meant,
like, actually a child

00:04:54.961 --> 00:04:58.798
would drive me on an ATV
across a cattle ranch.

00:04:58.798 --> 00:05:01.100
-We actually have a clip of
the scene you're talking about.

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:04.437
Here's Aidy Bryant in the
new season of "Shrill" on Hulu.

00:05:04.437 --> 00:05:05.971
Take a look.

00:05:05.971 --> 00:05:07.706
-Hi!

00:05:07.706 --> 00:05:09.508
[ Engine idling ]

00:05:09.508 --> 00:05:13.145
Uh, I'm here
to meet Clara Pickett.

00:05:13.145 --> 00:05:16.349
[ Engine idling ]

00:05:16.349 --> 00:05:18.751
Okay.

00:05:18.751 --> 00:05:22.254
Sorry.
I've never been one of these.

00:05:22.254 --> 00:05:26.726
So I'm gonna grab on there.
Okay.

00:05:26.726 --> 00:05:30.062
[Straining]
Just give it one of these.

00:05:30.062 --> 00:05:32.865
Okay. Okay.

00:05:32.865 --> 00:05:37.703
Um, is it okay if I put my hands
on your back here?

00:05:37.703 --> 00:05:40.239
Little support from a child.

00:05:40.239 --> 00:05:41.907
Okay.

00:05:41.907 --> 00:05:45.244
Ohh. [ Chuckles ]

00:05:45.244 --> 00:05:46.712
All right.

00:05:46.712 --> 00:05:49.282
So I'm good
to leave my car there?

00:05:49.282 --> 00:05:51.516
Okay.

00:05:51.516 --> 00:05:55.187
-Come on. Show business, man.
Happy early birthday.

00:05:55.187 --> 00:05:57.990
Aidy Bryant, everybody.
All episodes of the third

00:05:57.990 --> 00:06:01.694
and final season of "Shrill"
will be on Hulu this Friday.

